# Never let secrets, VCS metadata or test material into the build context;
# both the `api` and `confirm` targets do `COPY . .` in the builder stage,
# so anything not excluded here is a candidate for landing in the image.
#
# Pattern semantics, measured 25 September 2026 against Docker 29.8.0 and
# not assumed: a `.dockerignore` pattern is matched against the whole path
# relative to the context root with Go's `filepath.Match`, whose `*` does
# not cross a `/`. A bare `__pycache__/` therefore excludes `./__pycache__`
# and nothing else -- a probe context carrying `nested/__pycache__/x.txt`
# and `nested/.env` shipped both into the image under the old patterns, and
# shipped neither under the `**/` forms below. `**` matches zero directories
# too, so `**/__pycache__/` still covers the root-level one and the bare
# form is redundant rather than complementary. This is why every pattern
# that names a build artefact or a cache is written `**/`-prefixed.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Local environments and caches -- never shipped, and `.env*` may hold
# real secrets on a developer machine even though none is committed.
# `.venv` matters twice: the builder creates `/app/.venv` in the layer
# before `COPY . .`, so a host `.venv` reaching the context would overwrite
# a Linux venv with whatever ABI the developer's machine built.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.import_linter_cache/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
**/dist/
**/build/
**/*.egg-info/

# Test material and design docs: neither the API nor confirm runtime needs
# them, and the adversarial requirement is that they never reach the image,
# not merely that they are undocumented in it.
tests/
docs/
tools/

# `dev-docs/` is the threat model itself: the zero-trust plan with the
# A1..A11 attack scenarios and their unverified/residual rows, the design
# handoff, the implementation guide and eleven decision records, ~280 KB of
# it. It is gitignored, so a CI checkout never has it and its absence from
# this list was invisible there -- but CLAUDE.md's Commands section tells
# engineers to run `docker build --target api --platform linux/arm64 .` on
# their own machine, where the directory is present and `COPY . .` took it.
# Measured before this line existed: a probe file under `dev-docs/` was
# readable at `/app/dev-docs/` in the built `api` image. An attacker who
# reaches RCE in the read container should not also be handed the list of
# attacks this design already knows it does not stop.
dev-docs/

# Session working notes for the local model, also gitignored and also
# present on a developer machine. The glob covers the `.tmp-<pid>` file the
# maintaining hook writes before renaming over it. Measured: the 28 KB
# `handoff-for-local.md` shipped at `/app/handoff-for-local.md`.
handoff-for-local.md*

# The stub backend runs from the host source tree via a bind mount in
# docker-compose.yml (`backend-stub` uses the builder base image directly,
# not the `api`/`confirm` targets), so it never needs to be baked into
# either shipped image.
stub/

# Editor/agent metadata, never relevant to a production image. This also
# covers `.claude/worktrees/`, where concurrent sessions keep full second
# copies of this repository.
.claude/

# Brand assets: 212 KB of SVG and PNG with no runtime reader. Neither
# service serves them; the only reference anywhere is the `<img>` in
# README.md, which this file already excludes. `logos/README.md` shipped
# too under the old root-only patterns, which is the same bug as above.
assets/
logos/

# CI/CD definitions. No runtime value, and the deploy workflow names the
# secrets and the ECR/ECS shape an operator wires up; that belongs in the
# repository, not in a container an attacker may land in.
.github/

# Repo-management and internal-design files: no runtime value, and
# CLAUDE.md/README.md carry more of this project's internal security
# reasoning than a shipped container image should hold, even though none of
# it is a credential. `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock` are excluded from this
# list on purpose -- `uv sync` inside the image needs both. `migrations/`
# and `alembic.ini` are deliberately kept too: `alembic upgrade head` is
# run from this image as a one-off task, so dropping them would break a
# deploy path rather than harden one.
CLAUDE.md
README.md
Makefile
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.importlinter
.python-version
